# 🚩 Challenge: [Bit-O-Asm-1]
![alt text](bit-o-asm-1.png)
## 📝 Challenge Description
Can you figure out what is in the eax register? Put your answer in the academy flag format: academy{n} where n is the contents of the eax register in the decimal number base. If the answer was 0x11 your flag would be academy{17}. Download the assembly dump here.

Hints:
1. As with most assembly, there is a lot of noise in the instruction dump. Find the one line that pertains to this question and don't second guess yourself!.
---

### Code / Terminal Snippets
```bash
1. wget https://challenge-files.cylabacademy.net/library/f24a79de39123fb31928d2d4baf2de2385e587d089b95005083051f9afb90fa9/disassembler-dump0_a.txt
2. cat disassembler-dump0_a.txt
3. python
4. print(chr(0x30))

```

